# ES Learning architecture

Next.js App Router, React, TypeScript, and npm. Do not add NestJS or a backend unless a feature truly needs one.

- Pages and layout live in `src/app/`. Reusable UI lives in `src/components/`. Static copy lives in `src/data/`.
- Server Components are the default. Add `"use client"` only for state, events, or browser APIs.
- Keep the Figma home frame as the visual source of truth. Do not swap in a generic template, stock photos, or an icon library.
- Raster images are local WebP files. Icons and logos stay SVG under `public/assets/`.
- Forms validate in the browser. Do not invent a submit API.
- Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using Next.js APIs. This project is on Next.js 16.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — client boundary on a static section
"use client";
export function Impact() { /* markup only */ }

// ✅ GOOD — server section; motion stays in RevealLines
export function Impact() {
  return <section className="impact">…</section>;
}
```
